{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00236",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.26,
      "end_seconds": 5.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.57,
      "end_seconds": 9.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "No trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.71,
      "end_seconds": 21.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "Well, um, I've been feeling faint, and I wanted to get it checked. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.02,
      "end_seconds": 30.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.97,
      "end_seconds": 50.74,
      "duration_seconds": 19.77,
      "text": "I'd give it a seven, out of ten. I'd say once or twice a day. I notice it more with standing in the sun. Only sitting in the shade, and it's not much. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.1,
      "end_seconds": 53.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.14,
      "end_seconds": 62.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "A pounding headache goes along with it, most of the time. The pounding headache? That's been for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.65,
      "end_seconds": 65.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Have you had any fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.85,
      "end_seconds": 67.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "No. No fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.39,
      "end_seconds": 74.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, passing no urine, fever or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.54,
      "end_seconds": 77.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.51,
      "end_seconds": 84.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.65,
      "end_seconds": 100.72,
      "duration_seconds": 15.07,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure. I did try to ignore it for a while. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. Yes, heart disease. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.36,
      "end_seconds": 125.17,
      "duration_seconds": 20.81,
      "text": "Go on. Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.1,
      "end_seconds": 128.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Well, that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.62,
      "end_seconds": 130.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.03,
      "end_seconds": 136.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Just a stent put in my heart, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.66,
      "end_seconds": 138.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.41,
      "end_seconds": 152.2,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Aspirin. I take it once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.04,
      "end_seconds": 155.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Okay, how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.64,
      "end_seconds": 157.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "75 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.72,
      "end_seconds": 162.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.63,
      "end_seconds": 163.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.38,
      "end_seconds": 180.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.11,
      "end_seconds": 184.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Yes, sulfa drugs. I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.98,
      "end_seconds": 187.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.98,
      "end_seconds": 188.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.73,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.22,
      "end_seconds": 209.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.75,
      "end_seconds": 218.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.92,
      "end_seconds": 239.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 96 percent, BP is 94 over 63. And pulse 92, temp 36.5 degrees, respiratory rate 20."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.4,
      "end_seconds": 242.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.03,
      "end_seconds": 250.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.25,
      "end_seconds": 258.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.23,
      "end_seconds": 264.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.05,
      "end_seconds": 265.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.53,
      "end_seconds": 269.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.17,
      "end_seconds": 278.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Capillary refill is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.88,
      "end_seconds": 293.8,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.78,
      "end_seconds": 297.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Hold on, the screen's frozen for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.09,
      "end_seconds": 325.6,
      "duration_seconds": 18.51,
      "text": "Okay, that's done. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like heat exhaustion with some dehydration. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be an electrolyte imbalance, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.58,
      "end_seconds": 329.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Yeah, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.46,
      "end_seconds": 344.46,
      "duration_seconds": 14.0,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now heat exhaustion with some dehydration is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling faint, and no passing no urine or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.66,
      "end_seconds": 346.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.17,
      "end_seconds": 352.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.06,
      "end_seconds": 362.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "So, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.55,
      "end_seconds": 383.48,
      "duration_seconds": 19.93,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood salts for dehydration. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'll start you on ORS, 1 sachet, three times a day, for two days. You take it by mouth. That's for dehydration. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.59,
      "end_seconds": 391.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Uh, alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.61,
      "end_seconds": 412.14,
      "duration_seconds": 20.53,
      "text": "Avoid the midday sun for a few days and keep a water bottle with you. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. If you become confused or stop sweating, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Come back in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.93,
      "end_seconds": 413.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.38,
      "end_seconds": 418.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.49,
      "end_seconds": 424.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "So, you know, I come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.19,
      "end_seconds": 429.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.9,
      "end_seconds": 434.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.94,
      "end_seconds": 438.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}